      {
        "text": "Jason Dónes is a CPS parent from Humboldt Park. He is a former teacher who has taught in CPS schools. He serves as chief of people and operations at Beyond100K, a nonprofit working to diversify the STEM teaching workforce, and as Local School Council chair at Moos Elementary. He helped draft Illinois’ first set of culturally responsive teaching standards and worked on CPS’ Instructional Equity Working Group. He says he will push for budget transparency and work to increase budget resources for district schools. He also wants to protect CPS jobs that support immigrant students facing threats from immigration agents. He advocates for fully staffed schools, including nurses, counselors, and special education professionals.",
